index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..6156a16c7cdfcc866bbe7bc20fc8b085ba5d73d6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/output/branch-concepts/.work-v5/prompts/branch-03.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@
+Use case: compositing / precise-object-edit.
+EDIT TARGET AND PLACEMENT REFERENCE: refs/background.png (2880 x 1800). Create the added foreground illustration for this exact hero, keeping the same 8:5 canvas and coordinates. Return ONLY the new illustration on a truly transparent alpha canvas for lossless compositing over the original sky; do not reproduce the sky, clouds, logo, navigation or booking button. The original background is the immutable base.
+WHAT THIS IS: a single still frame of an SVG motion-design animation showing neural-network BACKPROPAGATION. The tree limb IS the neural network. It must read as a crisp flat VECTOR drawing constructed in Figma/Illustrator, NOT a photograph, not a realistic branch, not 3D.
+COMPOSITION in the 2880 x 1800 canvas: ONE thick limb enters cropped from the RIGHT EDGE with center at y=480 and thickness 260px (top approx y=350, bottom y=610). It extends LEFTWARD and fans into an irregular organic canopy, with leftmost small terminal nodes at x=1300 to 1450, y=420 to 680. Branches divide at uneven distances with asymmetric angles, unequal lengths, some sagging and one crossing. No central trunk, no roots or ground, no rigid diagram spacing. Keep branches around y=320-1050 on the right half. Fine hanging vines on the right half reach y=1450-1500, lower left always empty.
+KEEP OUT: whole y<250 band completely transparent, and rectangle x=0..1250,y=700..1800 completely transparent. All x<1250 preferably empty, no vines there. The original navigation and book meeting button must remain fully visible when composited.
+NEURAL STRUCTURE: obvious round ringed neuron nodes at every major fork, several different sizes (approx 24-75px), decreasing toward branch tips, small round output nodes terminating the twigs. Every limb contains a clean thin channel continuously connecting these nodes.
+BOTANICAL: stylised moss cushions along top surfaces as simplified green blobs; small graphic almond-shaped leaves, ivy, a few minimal ferns. Fine vertical hanging moss/vine strokes on the right half. Enough exposed channels and nodes to read the neural network. No detailed realistic foliage.
+TRAINING SIGNALS, unmistakable: cyan/white small capsule pulses moving FROM RIGHT EDGE toward LEFT TIPS, with short trails behind and tiny LEFT-POINTING arrow chevrons along channels. Three or four small output nodes at left tips show ORANGE LOSS halos. Orange capsules and tiny RIGHT-POINTING chevrons travel FROM ORANGE TIPS BACK RIGHT to the main limb; orange paths aggregate and become thicker and brighter approaching the right edge. Both forward cyan and backward orange signals simultaneously visible on separate parallel tracks where needed. Soft localized signal glows are allowed but hard crisp core strokes. Do not put detached icons or symbols around the drawing.
+STYLE: flat/semi-flat filled shapes, smooth clean bezier contours, rounded ends, consistent 2-6px outline strokes at final resolution. Limited palette deep navy #0b1a2b, white #ffffff, pale cyan #bff0ff, sky blues, moss greens #2f7d4f #59a96a #a9d18e, orange #ff7a2f solely for error signals. Flat tones or restrained simple vector gradients only. Premium sophisticated motion-design frame. The ORGANIC UNEVEN tree silhouette matters; no evenly spaced network tree.
+No added text, logos, labels, equations, numbers, watermark, UI or HUD. No photorealism, bark texture, photography, depth of field, metallic machinery, sci-fi pipes, or volumetric 3D.
+VARIATION 03: Duotone
+STRICT DUOTONE for all structure and plants: only deep navy #0b1a2b and one moss green #59a96a; no shaded green, no light green, no grey, no white structure, no gradients in structure. Cyan and orange may appear ONLY as signal cores, signal halos and loss node accents. Bold two-ink screenprint vector silhouettes, flat and clean.
