CRITICAL SILHOUETTE CORRECTION: Do NOT draw a balanced four-finger fan, fish skeleton, ladder, diamond lattice or neat parallel limbs. Draw a recognizably ORGANIC, GNARLED asymmetrical tree limb: the dominant stem bends down into a deep uneven S-curve before extending left; a SHORT fork turns sharply upward near the right input; one LONG slender offshoot doubles back and crosses behind a sagging lower limb; two unequal small twigs split much nearer the far-left tips. Use 6-9 terminal twigs with strongly unequal lengths and endpoints at scattered x,y positions, not a vertical row. Nothing is mirrored. Moss follows the upper surfaces. Ringed network nodes are INTEGRATED where branches fork, not arranged like circuit stations. No errors in directional arrows: EVERY CYAN chevron points toward its LEFT terminal. EVERY ORANGE chevron points along its path toward the RIGHT-edge input. Orange heads face RIGHT, with tails extending LEFT. Soft orange halos limited to very small zones, no diffuse haze elsewhere.
